1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,880
Nine merchant accounts. 129 payments. Not
one of them is unusual.

2
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:08,443
It only exists in what connects the
accounts.

3
00:00:08,443 --> 00:00:13,340
And every flag says why, in plain
language. A merchant can read it, and argue back.

4
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:17,973
Razorpay already scores every payment.
That model is good.

5
00:00:17,973 --> 00:00:23,307
But it is asked one question at a time. Is
this payment fine? Yes. Is this one? Yes.

6
00:00:23,307 --> 00:00:26,846
Nine correct answers. And the ring walks
straight through.

7
00:00:26,846 --> 00:00:30,360
The fraud was never inside a payment. It
is in what connects them.

8
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:35,220
Nine merchants. Each one, on its own,
looks completely fine.

9
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,486
Three of them sign in from the very same
device.

10
00:00:38,486 --> 00:00:41,200
Invisible if you look at payments one at a
time.

11
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,879
And three of them share a settlement
account.

12
00:00:43,879 --> 00:00:46,685
A marketplace shares an internet address
with its sellers.

13
00:00:46,685 --> 00:00:49,060
It does not put them on its own settlement
account.

14
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:54,984
Every account was opened inside the same
69 days. Real shops open over years.

15
00:00:54,984 --> 00:00:57,040
Mules are onboarded in a batch.

16
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:01,980
None of that is visible in any single
payment. All of it is visible in the group.

17
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:06,862
Now the results, on the half it was never
tuned on. 91 percent recall.

18
00:01:06,862 --> 00:01:12,651
87 percent precision. But 22 rings is a
small sample. The honest reading is a range.

19
00:01:12,651 --> 00:01:18,000
72 to 97 percent. And score.py prints that
interval beside every rate it reports.

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,566
But read the per class table, not the
headline. Nine classes of ring, all caught.

21
00:01:23,566 --> 00:01:26,640
And this one, recruiter quiet, 4 out of 5.

22
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:32,158
That one scores 67. My line is 70. I could
catch it by lowering the line.

23
00:01:32,158 --> 00:01:36,665
But two real family businesses sit at 67
and 63. Lowering it would flag them too.

24
00:01:36,665 --> 00:01:39,820
So it stays missed, and the reason is
written down.

25
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:44,197
I did not only plant criminals. I planted
innocents, to fool myself.

26
00:01:44,197 --> 00:01:47,162
A franchise chain on one settlement
account. A family on one device.

27
00:01:47,162 --> 00:01:51,296
And a brand opening six outlets in one
week, which looks exactly like a batch of

28
00:01:51,296 --> 00:01:53,760
mules. 20 legitimate groups. 0 flagged.

29
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:59,123
So how is that group found? Link any two
merchants that share an identifier.

30
00:01:59,123 --> 00:02:02,140
You get 221 thousand links, and one
useless blob.

31
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:06,494
Because 332 of them use the same email
provider. So, two rules.

32
00:02:06,494 --> 00:02:10,758
Drop what almost everyone shares. Make
every link earn its weight.

33
00:02:10,758 --> 00:02:14,600
That leaves 668 links, and 47 clean
groups. The largest is 9.

34
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:18,952
Timing is the strongest signal, and the
easiest to get wrong.

35
00:02:18,952 --> 00:02:23,341
Everybody is busy at Diwali. So nothing is
measured against a flat line.

36
00:02:23,341 --> 00:02:26,659
It is measured against what the book
itself did that day.

37
00:02:26,659 --> 00:02:31,097
On day 94, this ring did 21 percent of its
business. The book did half a percent.

38
00:02:31,097 --> 00:02:35,040
That is 39 times the rate, across 6
trading days in six months.

39
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:39,848
Then a second component argues with the
first. Six questions.

40
00:02:39,848 --> 00:02:46,405
Is this one weak attribute? A branded
chain? A marketplace? Ring R0025 scored 84.

41
00:02:46,405 --> 00:02:50,996
Verification cut it to 29, below the line.
Nobody is troubled.

42
00:02:50,996 --> 00:02:55,800
Verification has no path that raises a
score. The type itself rejects it.

43
00:02:56,700 --> 00:03:00,648
But what is each piece actually worth?
Take it out, and measure again.

44
00:03:00,648 --> 00:03:04,165
Removing the co-timing relation costs 27
points of recall.

45
00:03:04,165 --> 00:03:06,234
It is the most valuable idea here.

46
00:03:06,234 --> 00:03:09,940
Removing the money signal costs nothing,
and that row is in the table too.

47
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:14,566
I tested whether machine learning beats
the rules. It loses.

48
00:03:14,566 --> 00:03:16,065
And look at the tree it learned.

49
00:03:16,065 --> 00:03:20,283
The top split says densely connected
accounts are innocent. That is backwards.

50
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:24,480
It is explainable in the sense that you
can print it, and what it explains is false.

51
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:29,491
I also tested on Elliptic two. Real,
labelled Bitcoin subgraphs.

52
00:03:29,491 --> 00:03:34,099
I do not beat the published state of the
art. I land at the structure only baseline.

53
00:03:34,099 --> 00:03:38,340
Both of those are in the repo, because a
benchmark you only publish when you win is

54
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:39,340
not a benchmark.

55
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:42,728
17 checks. One for every claim I have
made.

56
00:03:42,728 --> 00:03:46,770
One scrambles every identifier and proves
the scores do not move.

57
00:03:46,770 --> 00:03:49,440
One proves the detector never opens the
answer key.

58
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:53,603
And this is the whole action ladder.
Observe. Watch. Review.

59
00:03:53,603 --> 00:03:58,185
And hold, a reversible one day settlement
delay that expires on its own.

60
00:03:58,185 --> 00:03:59,661
There is no freeze in this codebase.

61
00:03:59,661 --> 00:04:04,100
I cannot destroy a merchant's business by
accident. The function does not exist.

62
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:09,894
And this is not a simulation. 49 orders,
pulled live from the Razorpay API.

63
00:04:09,894 --> 00:04:14,388
2 rings found inside them. Now read the
last two lines of each. Both were refused.

64
00:04:14,388 --> 00:04:18,245
One attribute type, where two are
required. One run, where two are required.

65
00:04:18,245 --> 00:04:20,560
It found them, and it still would not act.

66
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:25,659
That is Ring Sentinel. 91 percent of rings
caught, on data it was never tuned on.

67
00:04:25,659 --> 00:04:27,214
None of the innocents flagged.

68
00:04:27,214 --> 00:04:31,516
And every number you have seen was
re-derived from the pipeline when this video was

69
00:04:31,516 --> 00:04:35,300
built. The worst thing it can do to a
merchant is make them wait one day.
